  "body": "Replacement for #3389. GitHub closed the original draft when the base branch of #3352 was deleted after merge. Main contains that parent. The original draft used commit `abed47739`. A trial merge with main at `6679b1b4b` was clean. The eight-file change on that tree has the same patch ID as the original change. On the trial merge `4afe34f02`, all five app `do_not_touch` tests and all six matching UI tests passed. They include the full tool sweep, tilted Trace refusal, blocked post, and viewport selection.\n\nTrace now accepts protected faces and edges. Generation checks the full tool along the selected line, including links and plunges. If a move cannot keep the requested clearance, generation refuses it and names the protected item. The post gate checks current protected geometry again. A Trace without protected items keeps its original moves.\n\n## Review fixes on `3980979a2`\n\nI merged upstream `main` at `6e641dac7` into the branch. Both reported failures reproduced on merge commit `d5353abf3`. The generated MCP reference was out of date. The click test could not arm the protected picker after the Geometry panel grew taller.\n\nI regenerated the reference with `camcraft-cli mcp reference`. The test now scrolls each control into view before it clicks. On the updated head, all six `mcp_doc_drift` tests and all three `do_not_touch_click` tests passed. The results for that head are replaced by the section below.\n\n## Conflict refresh on `6ad6311fa`\n\n`main` added Face to the \"Do not touch\" list. This PR adds Trace. Three files had a conflict: `crates/app/src/operation/types/avoid.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`. The merge commit `a26b7e16c` (`main` at `b48e05e5a`) keeps the two sides. The list is now Trace, 2D Offset, 3D Pocket and Face. Two later merges of `main` (`fdda55e15`, then `16dc39f06`) were clean and have no hand edits.\n\nQuick plan (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`), run one step for each test binary:\n\n- On head `bdf5a1588` (`main` at `fdda55e15`): 329 app steps ran and all 329 passed. They include the `camcraft-app` lib step. The 13 UI steps did not compile there because of a broken build cache on the host. That was not a code error.\n- On the final head `6ad6311fa` (`main` at `16dc39f06`): 23 steps ran again and all 23 passed.\n  - Pinning suites: `do_not_touch` (5 tests, Trace cases included), `do_not_touch_face` (3 tests), `mcp_doc_drift` (6 tests).\n  - `example_catalog` (37 passed, 4 ignored), `example_catalog_adaptive` (1), `example_catalog_edge_work` (1), `first_part_programs` (2).\n  - The three suites that the last merge of `main` added to the plan: `adaptive_pass_start` (4), `bore_pass_start` (3), `pocket_pass_start` (6).\n  - All 13 UI steps. The `camcraft-ui` lib step passed 1474 tests with 8 ignored. It includes the `do_not_touch` and `do_not_touch_click` tests.\n- The other 319 app steps did not run again on the final head.\n\nLight lane (`cargo xtask gate light`) on `6ad6311fa`: 3 steps, 0 failed (`light build`, `motion light: lib`, `motion light: adaptive_troch_parallel`).\n\nThe full heavy lanes did not run on this head. The rule of #3556 reserves them for the cut.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n**Trace Geometry before** (`6e641dac7`)\n\n![Trace Geometry before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/59db5a8401816032f74ef0791c3535d5823e2fe6/3462/3462-trace-before-main-6e641dac7.png)\n\n**Trace Geometry after selecting a protected face and edge** (`3980979a2`)\n\n![Trace Geometry after selecting a protected face and edge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/59db5a8401816032f74ef0791c3535d5823e2fe6/3462/3462-trace-after-3980979a2.png)\n\n**Verification on `abed47739`**\n\n- `trace_protects_the_full_sweep_between_clear_endpoints` failed on the parent when MCP refused protected items on Trace. It passes on this head.\n- The test places a protected face between two clear endpoints. The holder reaches it at a distance of 14.9 mm with a 15 mm clearance envelope. The shank reaches it at 6.9 mm with a 7 mm envelope. The clear case keeps the original moves. A refused path writes no NC file.\n- `tilted_trace_refuses_a_protected_face_in_its_work_plane` passes.\n- `trace_takes_a_protected_face_and_edge_by_viewport_click` passes with actual viewport clicks.\n- All 40 tests passed in the app suites `area_controls`, `do_not_touch`, `do_not_touch_project`, `engrave_law`, and `mill2d_b`. All six UI tests selected by `do_not_touch` passed. Clippy passed for all targets in the app and UI crates with warnings denied.\n\nAll 203 release-mode test steps selected by the heavy gate completed. The 26-step run covered the suites with ignored tests, the library, binary and doc steps, and the registered expected failures for #1950 and #2849. The other 177 steps also passed. The gate reported zero unexpected failures.\n\nThe heavy plan also lists one compile-only step for all 644 app integration targets. I built the reached targets separately on this host to fit the available disk. The change was not exercised on a physical machine.\n\nChangelog: Trace accepts protected faces and edges and refuses a path that cannot keep the full tool clear.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3348\n\n",
